ebcast":true,"url":"https://moderngov.harrow.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"LOBO loan forced refinancing: lender triggered rate reset which council declined, triggering \u00a320.8m prepayment","lead":"This crystallizes embedded refinancing risk: the council faced a lender-initiated rate increase beyond its control and was forced to execute a larger refinancing than planned. It demonstrates the council's vulnerability to non-standard debt terms and need\u2026","iso":"2026-07-20","paper_title":"12) Treasury Management Annual Outturn Report 2025-26 GARMS","paper_url":"https://harrow.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s201049/201049.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Capital programme delivered at only 33% of plan, with \u00a3150m of planned investment unspent","lead":"A 66% underspend signals either project deferrals or execution challenges that could affect the council's ability to deliver service improvements and efficiency gains. Lenders need confidence in capital programme delivery.","iso":"2026-07-20","paper_title":"12) Treasury Management Annual Outturn Report 2025-26 GARMS","paper_url":"https://harrow.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s201049/201049.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Council faces ongoing financial pressures in Adult Social Care and Temporary Housing","lead":"Acknowledged financial pressures in adult social care and temporary housing are significant budget drivers; their status is material to the council's financial forecast and borrowing position.","iso":"2026-07-20","paper_title":"15.1) Appendix 1 - Internal Audit Annual Report 2025-26 (Final)","paper_url":"https://harrow.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s201004/201004.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-07-20","committee":"Governance, Audit, Risk Management and Standards Committee","paper_title":"12) Treasury Management Annual Outturn Report 2025-26 GARMS","paper_url":"https://harrow.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s201049/201049.pdf","headline":"LOBO loan forced refinancing: lender triggered rate reset which council declined, triggering \u00a320.8m prepayment","detail":"The council's final remaining LOBO loan (Lender's Option, Borrower's Option) of \u00a320.8m had a rate reset triggered by the counterparty, who requested a higher interest rate. The council declined and repaid the loan using proceeds from \u00a365m of new PWLB borrowing at shorter term.","category":"borrowing","matters":"This crystallizes embedded refinancing risk: the council faced a lender-initiated rate increase beyond its control and was forced to execute a larger refinancing than planned. It demonstrates the council's vulnerability to non-standard debt terms and need to maintain sufficient liquidity for unplanned refinancing.","figures":"LOBO loan repaid \u00a320.8m; PWLB loans raised \u00a365m","quote":"During the year the council's final remaining LOBO loan counterparty triggered the option to request a higher interest rate. This was declined and the LOBO of \u00a320.8m was repaid.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-20","committee":"Governance, Audit, Risk Management and Standards Committee","paper_title":"12) Treasury Management Annual Outturn Report 2025-26 GARMS","paper_url":"https://harrow.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s201049/201049.pdf","headline":"Capital programme delivered at only 33% of plan, with \u00a3150m of planned investment unspent","detail":"The council planned \u00a3226.1m in capital expenditure but spent only \u00a375.6m (34% outturn). General Fund spent \u00a353.1m against \u00a3142.3m planned (37% outturn); HRA spent \u00a322.5m against \u00a383.8m planned (27% outturn). The document flags the variance but refers detailed analysis to a separate Revenue and Capital Outturn Report.","category":"capital","matters":"A 66% underspend signals either project deferrals or execution challenges that could affect the council's ability to deliver service improvements and efficiency gains. Lenders need confidence in capital programme delivery.","figures":"General Fund plan \u00a3142,287k actual \u00a353,064k; HRA plan \u00a383,783k actual \u00a322,530k; Total plan \u00a3226,070k actual \u00a375,594k","quote":"Total Capital Expenditure 226,070 75,594","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-20","committee":"Governance, Audit, Risk Management and Standards Committee","paper_title":"15.1) Appendix 1 - Internal Audit Annual Report 2025-26 (Final)","paper_url":"https://harrow.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s201004/201004.pdf","headline":"Council faces ongoing financial pressures in Adult Social Care and Temporary Housing","detail":"The Chief Audit Executive's opinion explicitly notes that the council is 'currently aware of issues that could affect its financial position such as, but not limited to, ongoing cost pressures associated with the delivery of Adult Social Care and Temporary Housing Accommodation.' These are named as known financial risks to the authority.","category":"demand","matters":"Acknowledged financial pressures in adult social care and temporary housing are significant budget drivers; their status is material to the council's financial forecast and borrowing position.","figures":"None provided in this audit report","quote":"The Council is currently aware of issues that could affect its financial position such as, but not limited to, ongoing cost pressures associated with the delivery of Adult Social Care and Temporary Housing Accommodation.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-20","committee":"Governance, Audit, Risk Management and Standards Committee","paper_title":"15.1) Appendix 1 - Internal Audit Annual Report 2025-26 (Final)","paper_url":"https://harrow.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s201004/201004.pdf","headline":"78 audit recommendations remain awaiting management response at report date","detail":"Of 121 recommendations due for implementation, only 43 had been fully or partially implemented by 30 June 2026. A substantial 78 recommendations were still pending management response when the report was issued, indicating slow or delayed implementation of audit findings across the council.","category":"audit","matters":"A high number of unresponded audit recommendations suggests the council may not be prioritising or moving quickly enough to remediate identified control weaknesses.","figures":"78 recommendations awaiting response; 43 of 121 due recommendations implemented (35%); 29 high and 163 medium recommendations made","quote":"There are 78 recommendations where a management response was pending at the time of reporting.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-20","committee":"Governance, Audit, Risk Management and Standards Committee","paper_title":"15.1) Appendix 1 - Internal Audit Annual Report 2025-26 (Final)","paper_url":"https://harrow.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s201004/201004.pdf","headline":"Six audit reviews received Limited Assurance ratings, indicating significant control weaknesses","detail":"Of 41 completed audits, 6 received Limited Assurance ratings covering IR35 (sole traders and agency), Planning Enforcement, Facilities Minor Works, SEN Travel Eligibility, and two education centres. Limited Assurance means 'a number of significant control weaknesses which could put the achievement of key service objectives at risk and result in error, fraud, loss or reputational damage' with high-priority recommendations indicating significant failings.","category":"audit","matters":"Control weaknesses in procurement, contractor management and school governance indicate areas where the council faces material operational and financial risk.","figures":"6 Limited Assurance reviews out of 41 completed; 17 high recommendations and 50 medium recommendations issued from Limited Assurance reviews","quote":"There are a number of significant control weaknesses which could put the achievement of key service objectives at risk and result in error, fraud, loss or reputational damage.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-07-30"},"name":"Harrow","findings_total":75,"news_drafts_total":3}}